                <pb facs="0568" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.504/2310a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-28">May 28, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>867. Justice has telegraphed the following instruction district directors of
                    immigration, “Effective immediately, nationals of Mexico are not to be admitted
                    as agricultural workers under the provisions of Public Law 45 and Regulations
                    8C4115 unless they present written consent of the Federal Government of Mexico
                    to emigrate for that purpose.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
